7:Entire Brain combines captured agent sessions and checkpoints with durable facts, documentation, and code understanding from [Entire Graph](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph). Graph maps how the code fits together; Brain connects that structure to why it exists, what happened before, and how to approach similar work.
68:Without Graph, `setup` reports the semantic index as unavailable; sessions, docs
126:Brain is set up per [repository](docs/reference.md#3a-what-setup-needs-first-and-what-it-does-not). Start in a local Git repository with at least one commit:
129:entire brain setup
132:By default, `setup` indexes the repository, extracts facts from up to 25 past sessions in the background, installs a watcher to keep the memory updated, and installs the agent instructions. The watcher runs as a persistent service on macOS and Linux with systemd.
134:The agent instructions live in these files, created or updated by `setup`:
136:- `.entire/agent-guide.md`: the agent instructions. Rerunning setup replaces this file.
140:product activates itself. `entire brain setup` on its own writes a
143:Run `entire graph setup` too if you want both.
145:The two setups compose in **either order**. The guide text is mirrored between
151:See the [agent integration guide](docs/reference.md#how-agents-use-the-brain) and [coordination contract](docs/agent-coordination.md) for more setup details.
160:entire brain setup --no-backfill --no-daemon
163:Configured remote history sources and hosted memories sync also use the network; see [privacy and egress](docs/reference.md#privacy-and-egress) for controls.
165:### Background maintenance and memory sync
167:The watcher updates local repository context and runs distillation within the configured budget.
168:For connected repositories, Brain syncs after a post-commit checkpoint notification and after distillation saves its results.
169:Existing push notifications and manual sync remain supported.
175:Failed or interrupted uploads remain eligible for the next sync event.
404:To stop and remove the watcher, run `entire brain setup --uninstall-daemon`. See [operations](docs/operations.md#after-the-install-onboard-a-repository) for service management.
418:| `entire brain setup` | Build the brain and start background updates |
423:| `entire brain connect` | Bind this repository to its hosted brain explicitly |
424:| `entire brain disconnect` | Stop syncing this repository with its hosted brain |
479:| `entire brain memories sync` | Sync repository memories with the hosted memory set (opt-in) |
